# Line-ending policy for the E1 data foundation.
#
# Why this file exists (E4-S1 audit finding):
# The E1-S6 manifest and the E1-S1 provenance record pin SHA-256 hashes for the
# raw artifact, the canonical dataset and the data dictionary. A hash is over
# BYTES, so any CRLF/LF conversion -- by git, by an editor, or by a sync tool --
# changes the hash even though not a single number changed. That silently
# disarms the integrity check the audit depends on.
#
# Keep the hashed artifacts byte-for-byte identical on every platform.

# Default: normalize text to LF inside the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Hash-pinned artifacts: never convert, in either direction.
*.csv   -text
*.json  -text

# Notebooks are JSON; converting them also breaks diffs and nbformat round-trips.
*.ipynb -text
